    "title": "Tiger Woods cozies up to Vanessa Trump in unearthed TikTok from Genesis Invitational",
    "text": "Vanessa Trump wrapped her arms around Tiger Woods for a cute photo op at the Genesis Invitational last weekend, as seen in a TikTok video. The golf legend, whose Tiger Woods Foundation hosted the tournament at Riviera Country Club in Los Angeles, showed some PDA with his girlfriend as they posed for photos on the course. She put her head on his shoulder as the five-time Masters champion held her waist. The former model, who is the ex-wife of Donald Trump Jr., was seen waving her hand for her daughter Kai Trump — a rising amateur golfer and University of Miami commit — to join the moment. They smiled for photographers while standing nearby a statue of golf icon Ben Hogan. Trump and her daughter also attended the Genesis Invitational at Torrey Pines Golf Course in La Jolla, Calif., last February. The mother-daughter duo have supported Woods at a number of events after he hard-launched his relationship with Vanessa in an Instagram post last March. Tiger Woods and girlfriend Vanessa Trump pose for photos together at the Genesis Invitational at Riviera Country Club from Feb 19-22, 2026. TikTok/jackiedluna626 (R to L) Tiger Woods, Vanessa Trump and Kai Trump pose for photos together at the Genesis Invitational at Riviera Country Club in greater Los Angeles. TikTok/jackiedluna626 Woods shared photos of the couple and asked the public for privacy, while Trump also reposted the message on her Instagram Story. The Post confirmed at the time that the two were taking things slow after their friendship blossomed into “something more.” Woods also made headlines over the weekend for his remarks on a potential return to this year’s Masters in April. Tiger Woods at the trophy ceremony on the 18th green during the final round of The Genesis Invitational 2026 at Riviera Country Club on February 22, 2026 in Pacific Palisades, Calif. Getty Images He said during the broadcast “there is” a chance he could return in time for The Masters. The 15-time major champion had surgery for a ruptured left Achilles last March.",
